<title>USA: Thermo Instrument gets most Life shares.</title>
<headline>Thermo Instrument gets most Life shares.</headline>
<dateline>WALTHAM, Mass. 1997-03-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>Thermo Instrument Systems Inc said Wednesday it had received acceptances representing about 85 percent of the outstanding shares of Life Sciences International Plc in its cash tender offer for all the company's shares.  </p>
<p>In January, Thermo made a recommended cash offer for the British company at 135p per share or a total of 235.9 million stg.</p>
<p>Thermo, which is 82-percent owned by Thermo Electron Corp, makes instruments used to detect and measure air pollution and other environmental hazards.</p>
<p>Life Sciences makes scientific equipment.</p>
</text>
